# Credits and attribution

## GBA Rush PSP Single-Game Launcher Builder

The launcher and its desktop builder were created by
[JxPv2](https://github.com/JxPv2) for the PSP homebrew community and inherited
through [andymcca/TempGBA4PSP-mod](https://github.com/andymcca/TempGBA4PSP-mod),
the direct upstream of GBA Rush PSP.

GBA Rush PSP maintains and distributes this component under a distinct fork
identity. That does not change its authorship or the licenses and notices
retained in this directory.

## Emulator lineage

- **2006** — **Exophase** creates
  [gpSP](https://github.com/PSP-Archive/gpsp), the emulator core at the
  foundation of this lineage.
- **2007-2009** — **Takka** and contributors develop
  [gpSP Kai](https://github.com/PSP-Archive/unofficial-gpSP-kai) for PSP.
- **2010-2012** — The **Supercard Team** ports the emulator to DSTwo as NDSGBA.
- **2013** — **Nebuleon**, **Normmatt**, **BassAceGold**, and contributors
  develop [TempGBA](https://github.com/PSP-Archive/TempGBA).
- **2013-2016** — TempGBA is brought back to PSP through TempGBA4PSP.
- **2016** — **Phoe-nix** creates
  [TempGBA4PSP-mod](https://github.com/phoe-nix/TempGBA4PSP-mod).
- **2024-2026** — [andymcca](https://github.com/andymcca) continues
  [TempGBA4PSP-mod](https://github.com/andymcca/TempGBA4PSP-mod), with launcher,
  interface, box-art, recent-ROM, and other contributions from
  [JxPv2](https://github.com/JxPv2) and additional contributors.
- **2026** — GBA Rush PSP begins as an independent fork of andymcca's
  repository, retaining this launcher and its attribution.

